Inheritance allows a class (subclass) to acquire the fields and methods of another class (superclass). Think of it like biology: a 'Dog' inherits traits from a generic 'Animal'. 

```java
class Animal { void eat() { System.out.println("Eating..."); } }
class Dog extends Animal { void bark() { System.out.println("Woof!"); } }
```
By using `extends`, the `Dog` class automatically gets the `eat()` method without rewriting it.

